A||||3||Rare87GT||Adding a Turbo to a 2.8L||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-25-2001||05:36 AM||||I know there are a few people on the boards here that have turboed there 2.8L.  What kind of times are the people that have done this running in the quarter mile?  Also has anyone ever added a Turbo off of a 89 or 90 TGP (Turbo Grand Prix).  Those engines have so much potential.  With a performance chip you can run 13's in a 3500lbs car.  Imagine that in a Fiero.  It would be an easy bolt on mod since they are both 60 degree engine.  Anyone have any resources on how to find some turbo setups from one of these Turbo Grand Prix.  Let me know some ideas.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-25-2001||06:52 AM||||If your more interested in 1/4 mile speed, your much better off to go with supercharger system. It gives imediate boost, turbos take too much time to spool up. There much better suited to power in a long run. Thats why you see lots more cars drag racing with superchargers and more long races with turbo powered cars. In my car, you cant hardly even feel any boost till youd be almost down the drag strip, then its like somebody gives you a big shove.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LoW_KeY||12-25-2001||07:12 AM||||Actually I read on a site that compared SC/TC and they said in the 1/4 you'd want a turbo, yes it lags off the line but they said once it kicks in the turbo will have a lot more pull through the gears then the SC.<P>If your racing around a track, SC you'll have the instant power right out of the corner.<P>Now a few things to look at..<P>Turbo will be cheap but produce a hefty amount of heat on your engine, best to go intercooled route.<P>SC expensive and you may have to sacrifice your A/C (big whoop)<P>I was thinking of one but then dropped it because I don't feel like spending money on something else that can go wrong when it breaks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-KC<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||chester||12-25-2001||09:36 AM||||I would assume that the style/model of turbo would determine the application to some extent.  Smaller turbo - faster spool up, less boost.  Bigger turbo - slower spool up, more boost.  Hybrid - best of both worlds. I'm planning a T3/4 hybrid install running 15 pounds of boost.  If lag turns out to be a problem then I'll juice it off the line  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Supercharger is out for me cause I'm one of those comfort orientated guys.  Want to lay down a spanking in the comfort of my A/C.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Should be a hell of a ride! <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
